And they kind of all freeze the TV and look at each other like, oh, my gosh, is that Aaron?

1197
00:57:01.440 --> 00:57:03.200
So it was a huge storyline.

1198
00:57:04.120 --> 00:57:05.440
Well, I remember, Angela.

1199
00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:09.740
And when I read that fan question, I went to the script as well.

1200
00:57:10.740 --> 00:57:16.340
And after they see the video, they realize she was born at this one particular hospital.

1201
00:57:16.340 --> 00:57:20.660
So her and Pete go take a walk in the neighborhood near the hospital.

1202
00:57:20.660 --> 00:57:26.300
And they wonder like, oh, is this maybe where she grew up?

1203
00:57:26.420 --> 00:57:28.260
Is this her background?

1204
00:57:28.940 --> 00:57:29.080
Right.

1205
00:57:29.220 --> 00:57:29.720
Her neighborhood.

1206
00:57:29.720 --> 00:57:35.980
But there's a very sweet line where in the nursery on the crib, the name just says St.

1207
00:57:36.140 --> 00:57:36.620
Margaret's.

1208
00:57:36.840 --> 00:57:40.920
And Aaron goes, oh, my original name was St.

1209
00:57:41.040 --> 00:57:41.520
Margaret's.

1210
00:57:41.580 --> 00:57:43.540
I guess I was a really religious baby.

1211
00:57:44.480 --> 00:57:46.200
And Phyllis is like, no, honey.

1212
00:57:46.700 --> 00:57:47.000
Yeah.

1213
00:57:47.140 --> 00:57:48.400
I think that's the church.

1214
00:57:49.800 --> 00:57:52.240
Well, we asked Dave Rogers about this.

1215
00:57:52.240 --> 00:57:59.520
And he sent us in an audio clip explaining why this entire storyline, this very elaborate storyline was cut.

1216
00:57:59.700 --> 00:58:00.900
Here's what he had to say.

1217
00:58:01.320 --> 00:58:10.760
You know, often in our episodes, we have scripts that are way, way longer than the time allotted to the final broadcast of the television show.

1218
00:58:10.900 --> 00:58:13.040
So a lot of stuff gets cut out.

1219
00:58:13.660 --> 00:58:19.020
Sometimes there's a beat here and there or a runner or a scene or multiple scenes.

1220
00:58:19.240 --> 00:58:27.820
In this case, we ended up removing an entire storyline from the episode, which had Aaron and Pete exploring Aaron being an orphan.

1221
00:58:28.540 --> 00:58:29.980
They go to talk to Phyllis.

1222
00:58:30.160 --> 00:58:31.560
This was a tricky story.

1223
00:58:31.920 --> 00:58:34.060
I think we all did our best to execute it.

1224
00:58:34.260 --> 00:58:36.820
And Jake and Ellie do a great job.

1225
00:58:37.140 --> 00:58:40.040
We really get to see them connecting in a nice way.

1226
00:58:40.040 --> 00:58:47.340
But ultimately, the story deals with Aaron being an orphan and not getting any closer to finding her parents or any other real information.

1227
00:58:48.420 --> 00:58:51.220
Just it wasn't very satisfying.

1228
00:58:51.660 --> 00:59:05.040
There's also a sad undertone between her being an orphan and Phyllis giving up a baby that it just it might have worked better in a supersized episode where the beats are a little bit more spread out while we have the comedy of the Dwight story.

1229
00:59:05.240 --> 00:59:09.620
But in a 21, 35 minute episode, it just felt really heavy.

1230
00:59:10.220 --> 00:59:16.120
I did let Ellie and Jake know that we ended up cutting it and I explained the same reasons I'm telling you now.

1231
00:59:16.300 --> 00:59:23.380
And I reassured them that what they were doing together was great and to keep doing it as their storyline keeps moving on.

1232
00:59:23.620 --> 00:59:32.640
But this was just a matter of this particular story and the time that we had for the show and that we just couldn't trim out a beat here or there in their story.

1233
00:59:32.780 --> 00:59:34.900
It was like every beat depended on the beat before.

1234
00:59:35.060 --> 00:59:35.920
It was very linear.

1235
00:59:37.320 --> 00:59:38.660
So that's what happened.

1236
00:59:38.660 --> 00:59:55.980
And we ended up cutting this whole storyline out and just focused more on Dwight and his freaky friends and had a little room in there for the Pam, Brian, Jim relationship arc.

1237
00:59:57.260 --> 01:00:01.240
You know, it is so like Dave to reach out to us.

1238
01:00:01.600 --> 01:00:07.380
If he ever had to cut something that we had done, he would always reassure us.

1239
01:00:07.540 --> 01:00:08.400
He was so thoughtful.

1240
01:00:08.400 --> 01:00:10.380
Just so you know, this wasn't your performance.

1241
01:00:11.080 --> 01:00:11.260
Yeah.

1242
01:00:11.520 --> 01:00:13.100
This was a story thing.

1243
01:00:13.240 --> 01:00:14.320
This was a time thing.

1244
01:00:14.480 --> 01:00:15.240
This was a whatever.

1245
01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:18.440
We just didn't have time to tell this story.

1246
01:00:19.100 --> 01:00:19.480
Yeah.

1247
01:00:19.640 --> 01:00:21.180
He's a stand up guy that way.

1248
01:00:21.600 --> 01:00:21.840
Yeah.

1249
01:00:22.440 --> 01:00:27.700
Now Dwight is going to interview Wolf, but this interview goes off the rails really quickly.

1250
01:00:28.100 --> 01:00:29.620
Yeah, it really does.

1251
01:00:29.620 --> 01:00:32.060
And I think Dwight's starting to get nervous.

1252
01:00:32.060 --> 01:00:33.940
He's now going to interview Hede.

1253
01:00:34.460 --> 01:00:34.840
Yeah.

1254
01:00:34.980 --> 01:00:36.500
And that doesn't work out either.

1255
01:00:36.800 --> 01:00:44.460
So Dwight is in the conference room and he's got this sort of like cork board and he has the name of all the different applicants on the board.

1256
01:00:44.460 --> 01:00:48.200
And he's saying, I just can't seem to decide.

1257
01:00:48.640 --> 01:00:50.500
Here's the little tidbit I teased earlier.

1258
01:00:50.800 --> 01:00:52.700
And remember when we were at lunch?

1259
01:00:52.900 --> 01:00:53.680
With Dave.

1260
01:00:53.880 --> 01:00:54.100
Yeah.

1261
01:00:54.360 --> 01:00:54.780
Yes.

1262
01:00:54.980 --> 01:00:59.420
And he told us how they didn't confirm Rolf for the episode.

1263
01:00:59.420 --> 01:01:07.120
They didn't have James Urbaniak confirmed to be in the episode until after we already started shooting the episode.

1264
01:01:07.560 --> 01:01:07.900
Yeah.

1265
01:01:08.020 --> 01:01:10.280
He wasn't even on set till like day two or something.

1266
01:01:10.280 --> 01:01:11.000
Yes.

1267
01:01:11.340 --> 01:01:23.640
But Dave told us he was so hopeful that it would work out that he shot this scene with a blank note card up in the corner and he wrote Rolf on it in poSt.

1268
01:01:24.180 --> 01:01:25.000
That's right.

1269
01:01:25.140 --> 01:01:25.820
That's right.

1270
01:01:26.040 --> 01:01:29.760
He put a little placeholder just in case they got him on that cork board.

1271
01:01:30.220 --> 01:01:30.500
Yes.

1272
01:01:31.200 --> 01:01:32.460
Dwight's in a tough spot now.

1273
01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:35.700
He's actually kind of rolling around on the floor in Andy's office.

1274
01:01:35.920 --> 01:01:36.320
Mm-hmm.

1275
01:01:36.520 --> 01:01:39.620
And Melvina wants to know if he needs to be changed.

1276
01:01:39.620 --> 01:01:41.780
He says, no, he does that himself now.

1277
01:01:42.060 --> 01:01:46.940
And she says, well, are you going to have a decision soon because I've been double parked for five hours?

1278
01:01:47.560 --> 01:01:49.920
And Dwight's like, no, your car's been towed by now.

1279
01:01:51.560 --> 01:01:59.840
And then a few more of his friends come in and they promise, listen, no matter who you choose, we'll still be your friend.

1280
01:01:59.840 --> 01:02:07.760
And Dwight's like, yeah, I mean, even if I choose none of you, they say, well, that wouldn't happen.

1281
01:02:08.000 --> 01:02:12.500
You wouldn't drag us all down here and waste all of our time to pick none of us.

1282
01:02:12.860 --> 01:02:14.140
Yeah, that would be insulting.

1283
01:02:14.780 --> 01:02:17.920
So Dwight is going to have to team up with Jim.

1284
01:02:18.360 --> 01:02:18.840
Yes.

1285
01:02:18.960 --> 01:02:21.700
He's going to seek out his enemy because he has no choice.

1286
01:02:21.960 --> 01:02:26.120
And he says, Jim, will you please pick someone?

1287
01:02:26.740 --> 01:02:30.560
And he basically says, I don't want to hire any of these people.

1288
01:02:30.780 --> 01:02:34.640
You can hire Clark, but you have to break the news to everyone.

1289
01:02:34.640 --> 01:02:37.120
And we're going to make it seem like it was your decision.

1290
01:02:37.120 --> 01:02:42.900
Dwight says, it turns out my standards for co-workers are higher than my standards for friends.

1291
01:02:43.260 --> 01:02:46.320
He couldn't imagine any of them in the old golden gray.

1292
01:02:46.740 --> 01:02:50.340
And yes, he did design uniforms for Dunder Mifflin.

1293
01:02:50.680 --> 01:02:53.660
Hey, as a talking head, he shows us the uniforMs.

1294
01:02:53.660 --> 01:02:56.780
They are summer, winter, jungle, and formal.

1295
01:02:57.300 --> 01:03:03.040
We got a fan question from Megan B in Toronto and Martha B in Malta who said,

1296
01:03:03.040 --> 01:03:08.220
who drew the Dunder Mifflin uniforms and were they given any instructions by the writers?

1297
01:03:08.780 --> 01:03:12.000
Well, this was such a quick pop, but I loved it so much.

1298
01:03:12.160 --> 01:03:13.180
I went to the script.

1299
01:03:13.380 --> 01:03:16.720
There was not a description for these drawings in the script.

1300
01:03:17.620 --> 01:03:22.220
Steve Burgess thinks that Alicia, our costume designer, might have drawn these.

1301
01:03:22.720 --> 01:03:24.380
And we asked Dave Rogers.

1302
01:03:24.380 --> 01:03:28.780
He couldn't remember who drew them, but he did have a fun tidbit to share.

1303
01:03:28.980 --> 01:03:30.000
Here's what he said.

1304
01:03:31.060 --> 01:03:36.300
One of the things that was really fun was Dwight's talking head where he shows off,

1305
01:03:36.340 --> 01:03:40.820
you know, sketches of Dunder Mifflin uniforms that he designed.

1306
01:03:41.360 --> 01:03:46.440
I do remember giving small notes to color them in so they'd read better on camera,

1307
01:03:46.560 --> 01:03:48.720
that they weren't just like, you know, pencil sketches.

1308
01:03:49.560 --> 01:03:52.140
What's really interesting is that when we got into editing,

1309
01:03:52.740 --> 01:03:55.000
Greg actually thought they were too fashionable.

1310
01:03:55.420 --> 01:03:57.580
And he had us reshoot with new versions.

1311
01:03:57.580 --> 01:04:00.340
And so we had alternate versions.

1312
01:04:00.520 --> 01:04:06.480
We shot a new version of the talking head where the uniforms really leaned more into the military.

1313
01:04:06.920 --> 01:04:11.580
The summer outfit was practically a, how do you pronounce it, a Geely suit.

1314
01:04:12.540 --> 01:04:15.800
But after seeing the new costumes, he changed his mind.

1315
01:04:16.360 --> 01:04:19.040
And so he liked the original costumes better.

1316
01:04:19.040 --> 01:04:21.300
And that's what you see in the show.

1317
01:04:21.700 --> 01:04:25.740
I think I have pictures of the alternate ones.

1318
01:04:25.740 --> 01:04:27.440
I will send that to you guys.

1319
01:04:28.200 --> 01:04:29.860
So Dave is so amazing.

1320
01:04:29.860 --> 01:04:30.800
And you know what?

1321
01:04:30.860 --> 01:04:32.360
He saves everything too, Jenna.

1322
01:04:32.580 --> 01:04:33.900
We're kind of both like that.

1323
01:04:34.020 --> 01:04:35.980
You are digital clutter buddies.

1324
01:04:36.220 --> 01:04:36.900
We are.

1325
01:04:37.120 --> 01:04:38.240
Except his are organized.

1326
01:04:39.040 --> 01:04:39.800
It's true.

1327
01:04:40.140 --> 01:04:42.860
But, you know, I looked at all of those sketches,

1328
01:04:42.860 --> 01:04:47.640
and they did remind me so much of the sketches that I saw Alicia do over the years.

1329
01:04:47.880 --> 01:04:48.600
Me too.

1330
01:04:49.080 --> 01:04:49.780
She's such a good artiSt.

1331
01:04:49.780 --> 01:04:51.560
And it had her sort of style.

1332
01:04:51.560 --> 01:04:53.420
So I feel like they were hers.

1333
01:04:53.720 --> 01:04:56.300
But I will put them in stories so you guys can all see.

1334
01:04:57.080 --> 01:05:00.060
Next up, Jim is going to break the news to all of the applicants.

1335
01:05:00.280 --> 01:05:02.580
He says, I am hiring none of you.

1336
01:05:03.960 --> 01:05:05.700
Dwight pretends to be outraged.

1337
01:05:05.920 --> 01:05:07.100
Jim's like, tone it down.

1338
01:05:07.380 --> 01:05:07.800
Tone it down.

1339
01:05:07.900 --> 01:05:08.980
Yes, exactly.

1340
01:05:09.920 --> 01:05:12.420
Ralph is like, I know what this was.

1341
01:05:12.700 --> 01:05:14.360
I know you're behind this.

1342
01:05:14.360 --> 01:05:18.740
I wouldn't open any suspicious packages, or maybe you should open them.

1343
01:05:19.000 --> 01:05:20.780
You do not want to cross, Ralph.

1344
01:05:21.080 --> 01:05:22.040
You do not.

1345
01:05:22.320 --> 01:05:24.280
All of Dwight's friends start to leave,

1346
01:05:24.380 --> 01:05:26.960
and they're kind of unsure what they're going to do for the rest of the day.

1347
01:05:27.240 --> 01:05:29.900
Then they decide to go paintball without Dwight.

1348
01:05:30.100 --> 01:05:30.980
He is bummed.

1349
01:05:31.320 --> 01:05:35.220
And Creed, as they leave, kind of sneakily joins them in leaving.

1350
01:05:36.040 --> 01:05:40.660
Yes, we got a fan catch from Emily B in San Diego and St. Louis,

1351
01:05:41.280 --> 01:05:46.720
who said, I'm not the best at fan catches, so I was pretty darn proud of myself for noticing this one.

1352
01:05:47.340 --> 01:05:53.100
Dwight's friends all leave to play paintball, and we see Creed run out after them, presumably to join them.

1353
01:05:53.200 --> 01:05:58.180
But when Dwight later gets an email with a picture of the group, Creed isn't in the photo.

1354
01:05:59.060 --> 01:06:02.400
Maybe Creed just used the opportunity to get out of work early.

1355
01:06:03.180 --> 01:06:04.580
Emily, I think you're right.

1356
01:06:04.760 --> 01:06:07.000
I think Creed was just a plain hooky.

1357
01:06:07.680 --> 01:06:08.700
No, ladies.

1358
01:06:08.700 --> 01:06:10.620
Please, he actually went.

1359
01:06:11.220 --> 01:06:12.780
But he's not in the picture.

1360
01:06:13.180 --> 01:06:14.200
I know.

1361
01:06:14.460 --> 01:06:16.220
Here's how it was in the shooting draft.

1362
01:06:16.400 --> 01:06:20.640
There was a tag written for the episode where they all go and play paintball,

1363
01:06:20.840 --> 01:06:23.700
and it said, exterior paintball field day.

1364
01:06:24.640 --> 01:06:29.680
Creed is on his knees, begging for his life as Wolf holds a paintball gun to his head.

1365
01:06:30.060 --> 01:06:31.240
Gabor stands nearby.

1366
01:06:31.840 --> 01:06:35.220
It's also in deleted scenes, and I'm going to play it for you.

1367
01:06:37.090 --> 01:06:40.730
Please, I don't know where my teammates are or what we're doing.

1368
01:06:40.970 --> 01:06:41.710
Is this a game?

1369
01:06:41.810 --> 01:06:42.470
Am I having fun?

1370
01:06:42.670 --> 01:06:45.670
He doesn't need to tell us what he's thinking, so I can read his mind.

1371
01:06:48.600 --> 01:06:50.640
It helps if you kind of mouth what you're thinking.

1372
01:06:50.880 --> 01:06:51.440
Hey, guys.

1373
01:06:51.780 --> 01:06:53.060
There's a creek over there.

1374
01:06:53.280 --> 01:06:55.060
And, well, I almost drowned.

1375
01:06:56.340 --> 01:06:57.560
Ah, Wolf!

1376
01:06:57.800 --> 01:06:59.000
I'm on your team!

1377
01:07:00.560 --> 01:07:01.120
Wolf!

1378
01:07:01.500 --> 01:07:04.520
Wolfman's gone rogue, and now you die.

1379
01:07:04.820 --> 01:07:07.460
Okay, I'll tell everyone everything.

1380
01:07:07.780 --> 01:07:10.620
The hobbit and the old woman are hiding in the port-a-potty.

1381
01:07:10.860 --> 01:07:14.580
Oh, my gosh!

1382
01:07:14.580 --> 01:07:18.820
So I knew about this tag, lady, but I didn't know Creed was in it.

1383
01:07:18.820 --> 01:07:22.480
Yes, and Creed ultimately gives up Melvina and Troy.

1384
01:07:22.780 --> 01:07:24.740
I guess they were hiding in the port-a-potty, like he said.

1385
01:07:24.980 --> 01:07:26.640
But here's my theory.

1386
01:07:27.060 --> 01:07:28.800
I think Creed took the picture.

1387
01:07:29.460 --> 01:07:31.000
Oh, that's good.

1388
01:07:31.720 --> 01:07:32.320
Uh-huh.

1389
01:07:32.560 --> 01:07:33.400
I like that.

1390
01:07:33.400 --> 01:07:34.900
That's why he wasn't in it.

1391
01:07:35.060 --> 01:07:39.680
And, you know, when we had lunch with Dave, he told us shooting these paintball tag scenes

1392
01:07:39.680 --> 01:07:40.600
were his favorite.

1393
01:07:40.880 --> 01:07:41.180
I know.

1394
01:07:41.180 --> 01:07:42.380
He loved it so much.

1395
01:07:42.640 --> 01:07:46.280
He said it was just so fun to shoot something that had some action, you know?

1396
01:07:46.280 --> 01:07:50.240
But they ultimately didn't use it, but it is all in deleted scenes.

1397
01:07:51.020 --> 01:07:53.840
Listen, I think that the episode ends perfectly.

1398
01:07:53.860 --> 01:07:57.300
I think that this tag was probably really funny.

1399
01:07:57.780 --> 01:07:59.440
And fun to do, right?

1400
01:07:59.540 --> 01:08:01.560
They all got to be outside running around.

1401
01:08:01.900 --> 01:08:02.220
Yeah.

1402
01:08:02.420 --> 01:08:04.840
But, ooh, the way it ended was so powerful.

1403
01:08:05.200 --> 01:08:06.440
All right, we're almost there.

1404
01:08:06.620 --> 01:08:08.040
We are almost there.

1405
01:08:08.400 --> 01:08:12.500
Clark gets the job, and Jim is going to help him get all set up at his desk.

1406
01:08:13.020 --> 01:08:14.700
Pam comes back from the warehouse.

1407
01:08:14.700 --> 01:08:18.380
She's very happy that it's Clark and not one of Dwight's friends.

1408
01:08:20.120 --> 01:08:22.820
And Jim's going to leave and go back to Philly.

1409
01:08:23.540 --> 01:08:27.040
Yeah, Jim kisses her goodbye, and he leaves.

1410
01:08:27.540 --> 01:08:31.120
They're kind of sitting there in their new clump, and Clark says to Pam,

1411
01:08:31.220 --> 01:08:32.060
hey, I'm going to the kitchen.

1412
01:08:32.160 --> 01:08:32.840
You want anything?

1413
01:08:33.260 --> 01:08:35.220
I think that's a good desk mate.

1414
01:08:35.760 --> 01:08:36.720
Very nice.

1415
01:08:37.040 --> 01:08:37.240
Yeah.

1416
01:08:37.720 --> 01:08:39.080
Pam says she's okay.

1417
01:08:39.100 --> 01:08:41.260
Dwight says, I would love some more coffee.

1418
01:08:41.260 --> 01:08:46.580
But then Clark says, oh, sorry, you have to be this tall for coffee.

1419
01:08:46.720 --> 01:08:50.600
Or he calls back that little bit that Dwight did to him in the break room earlier.

1420
01:08:51.080 --> 01:08:52.900
Yeah, Dwight's not cool enough for coffee.

1421
01:08:53.200 --> 01:08:53.560
Yeah.

1422
01:08:54.160 --> 01:08:58.840
So Pam sees that Dwight is sad, and she says, hey, do you want to haze the new guy?

1423
01:08:59.700 --> 01:09:01.740
Dwight is so tickled.

1424
01:09:02.160 --> 01:09:04.440
Pam's like, okay, here's some saran wrap.

1425
01:09:04.640 --> 01:09:06.180
Next time Clark goes to the bathroom.

1426
01:09:06.320 --> 01:09:07.100
And Dwight interrupts her.

1427
01:09:07.100 --> 01:09:08.040
He's like, no, no, don't worry.

1428
01:09:08.140 --> 01:09:08.860
I know what to do.

1429
01:09:08.980 --> 01:09:10.480
And they kind of get tickled.

1430
01:09:10.780 --> 01:09:16.300
And then Clark returns to his desk, and Dwight covers his face in saran wrap.

1431
01:09:16.720 --> 01:09:18.180
This is not the toilet.

1432
01:09:18.380 --> 01:09:19.860
Pam meant the toilet trick.

1433
01:09:20.180 --> 01:09:25.260
So, lady, I remember reading this, and I remember thinking, we're going to kill Clark.

1434
01:09:26.220 --> 01:09:27.320
We're going to kill him.

1435
01:09:27.440 --> 01:09:33.460
Because, I mean, Rain admitted that he would really go for it in scenes like this.

1436
01:09:33.600 --> 01:09:35.160
Yes, he goes all out.

1437
01:09:35.160 --> 01:09:39.840
Yes, so when we were planning this scene, I was like, we need a signal.

1438
01:09:40.120 --> 01:09:41.940
We need a safe word.

1439
01:09:42.200 --> 01:09:48.960
We need some way that we know the difference between Clark acting and Clark actually suffocating.

1440
01:09:49.860 --> 01:09:53.360
We also asked Dave about this scene, and here's what he had to say.

1441
01:09:54.500 --> 01:09:58.380
Rain fully commits to being Dwight in his performance every time.

1442
01:09:58.520 --> 01:10:02.620
And I remember being a little nervous when reading the script, and it said Dwight was

1443
01:10:02.620 --> 01:10:04.380
going to wrap Clark's head in shrink wrap.

1444
01:10:04.720 --> 01:10:07.840
So, of course, we get to set, and everyone is there telling me, we need to watch Clark

1445
01:10:07.840 --> 01:10:09.020
and make sure he can breathe.

1446
01:10:09.300 --> 01:10:11.000
Like, everybody's just anxious and nervous.

1447
01:10:11.020 --> 01:10:16.540
So, it builds up all this anxiety for this, you know, really small, I mean, I wouldn't

1448
01:10:16.540 --> 01:10:21.400
call it a stunt, you know, this physical action between two actors, you know, on a

1449
01:10:21.400 --> 01:10:23.560
controlled set, our little office set.

1450
01:10:23.880 --> 01:10:26.240
I will say that they shot take one.

1451
01:10:26.400 --> 01:10:27.620
It looked pretty good to me.

1452
01:10:28.100 --> 01:10:30.080
And when we cut, they were both laughing.

1453
01:10:30.280 --> 01:10:31.600
And then Rain asked, you know, you okay?

1454
01:10:31.740 --> 01:10:33.240
And Clark was like, oh, yeah, that was fine.

1455
01:10:33.320 --> 01:10:34.480
You can go even more than that.

1456
01:10:34.940 --> 01:10:37.580
So, you know, they did several takes.

1457
01:10:37.920 --> 01:10:40.520
The two of them really had fun doing the gag.

1458
01:10:41.080 --> 01:10:45.780
Clark was never in any real danger, but he sold it, that he was, you know, choking and

1459
01:10:46.420 --> 01:10:50.640
suffocating, and, you know, it was just, to me, I was really happy with how it came

1460
01:10:50.640 --> 01:10:50.800
out.

1461
01:10:50.880 --> 01:10:53.060
It came out, you know, really, really funny.

1462
01:10:54.080 --> 01:10:56.120
It was so realistic to me.

1463
01:10:56.140 --> 01:11:00.460
I had forgotten this moment, you know, and then in our rewatch, I felt like I saw it for

1464
01:11:00.460 --> 01:11:02.040
the first time, and I was like, ah!

1465
01:11:02.720 --> 01:11:06.740
I was in full panic attack mode the entire time we shot this scene.

1466
01:11:06.780 --> 01:11:07.520
Oh, I bet.

1467
01:11:08.540 --> 01:11:09.420
They sold it.

1468
01:11:09.420 --> 01:11:12.680
My performance is my real reaction.

1469
01:11:14.240 --> 01:11:17.260
All right, are we ready for the final moment?

1470
01:11:17.980 --> 01:11:20.240
Yeah, here it comes.

1471
01:11:20.840 --> 01:11:22.880
Jim is going to have a talking head.

1472
01:11:23.500 --> 01:11:27.360
He says, of course it matters who sits next to Pam.

1473
01:11:27.780 --> 01:11:30.800
Who you sit next to is who you spend your life with.

1474
01:11:31.340 --> 01:11:35.060
He fell in love because he spent all those years staring at Pam.

1475
01:11:35.060 --> 01:11:44.660
And then the camera reveals Brian holding a boom over Pam and just looking at her with

1476
01:11:44.660 --> 01:11:46.680
such adoration and smiling.

1477
01:11:47.080 --> 01:11:53.220
And Jim's last line of his talking head is, that stuff definitely matters.

1478
01:11:54.080 --> 01:11:57.320
I mean, people lost their minds.

1479
01:11:57.700 --> 01:11:58.020
Mm-hmm.

1480
01:11:58.880 --> 01:11:59.100
Yeah.

1481
01:12:00.620 --> 01:12:07.220
Turns out, maybe Brian and Alyssa's marriage isn't as strong as we thought it was.

1482
01:12:07.920 --> 01:12:10.300
He definitely likes looking at Pam.

1483
01:12:10.900 --> 01:12:14.780
I have one funny behind-the-scenes detail about this moment.

1484
01:12:14.980 --> 01:12:15.780
What is it?

1485
01:12:15.980 --> 01:12:18.040
I remember when you guys were doing it.

1486
01:12:18.040 --> 01:12:18.980
We were there.

1487
01:12:18.980 --> 01:12:20.660
I was over in the accounting nook.

1488
01:12:20.660 --> 01:12:23.580
